. With the incumbent term-limited, neither side carries an incumbency advantage, and no general-election polls or expert ratings are yet available, leaving fundamentals to drive the outlook.\n\nRecent headlines highlight Alaska's growing competitiveness: Democrats are running strong in the state's Senate and House contests, and some observers ask whether it could become a swing state. But that strength has not yet been demonstrated at the presidential level, where Republicans have consistently led. The Republican edge stands near six points, with wide uncertainty until polling arrives.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2436, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3013, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2918, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3121, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2994, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.311, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2901, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2902, "margin": -6.0}]}